Design notes (parity + native idiom):
  - Foundation JSONSerialization cannot preserve object key order; JSON.stringify never reorders.
    => hand-written strict scanner keeps member order; printer matches JS exactly (2-space indent,
       integer numbers without trailing ".0", -0 -> "0", control-char \u00xx escaping, raw "/" + UTF-8,
       duplicate key keeps first position + last value). 11 adapter assertions pin these.
  - No data hook (only useTranslation) => the real branches are empty / error / formatted. There is no
    async source, so loading/stale/offline do not exist in the source and are not fabricated (Honesty
    rule 2/3: reproduce the source's actual branches, do not invent surfaces).
  - Telemetry: model.start() emits view.opened (surface slug "JsonFormatter") once, idempotent.

